comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T04:46:55.032Z","harness:claude-code","Investigation note: auditMergeAttributeFence walks up to eight filesystem parents of the tracker root and accepts the first .gitattributes holding a managed block, with no Git-root bound. All three callers share it: health (resolveMergeFenceHealthEvidence), validate (validate_merge_fence_drift) and the workspace position read. Plan: an optional gitWorkspaceRoot bound, compared by realpath per level so a symlinked logical path keeps its tracker-relative patterns; directories outside the bound are never read. Callers pass the git root they already resolve; a tracker outside Git keeps the bounded walk."
  "2026-11-20T04:50:13.037Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence: the GH-1759 shell reproduction against this branch's dist now reports git check-attr merge unspecified, strict health exit 1 with failed_because merge_fence_missing:1; restoring the inner fence gives exit 0, ok true, 0 warnings. The new real-Git spec covers that layout, a fence in an in-repository directory between the root and the tracker (still counted), a symlinked logical tracker path (same fence, same patterns), a boundary that does not hold the tracker, and an unresolvable tracker directory. Negative control: with the boundary check disabled both tests fail at the not_installed expectation (the outer fence is accepted as ok)."
